{
  "title": "Windows Server Basis",
  "uid": "system-1229",
  "tags": [
    "onboarding",
    "platform"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "Environment",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "PROD : prod",
        "current": {},
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "host",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
        "query": "label_values(Processor_Processor_Time_ratio, host_name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "description": "Filters every per-host panel below - same fleet-scale reasoning as the Linux Basis dashboard's $host variable."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "System",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Windows Server Basis** (`1229`, type `platform`)\n\nTenant: `1229-${env}`\n\nOwner: Platform Engineering (platform-team@example.com)\n\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Configured Ingestion Budget",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**PROD**: 30 GB total (1 GB/day x 30 days retention, size `S`)\n\nRendered from the manifest at generation time - not a live query. See **Ingestion Budget Usage** alongside for the live percentage."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Ingestion Budget Usage (per Signal)",
      "description": "This tenant's real ingested volume since local midnight (Europe/Zurich), as a percentage of EACH signal's own daily budget - Metrics (Mimir), Logs (Loki), Traces (Tempo), Profiles (Pyroscope) each shown as its own line. Both values read directly from two gauges scripts/ingestion-midnight-snapshot.py pushes every 2 minutes (demo_ingestion_since_midnight, demo_ingestion_daily_budget) - no subtraction on this panel's own side (NFR-05 SECOND pre-test audit round, fixed here: this used to recompute \"current minus a separately-pushed day-start snapshot\" in this panel's OWN PromQL, independently of - and able to silently disagree with - the enforcer's own decision, with its own version of that script's pre-fix reset-insensitivity; both now read the exact same, already-correct value). Green below 80%, yellow 80-90%, red above 90%. Same formula as the Operator: Tenant Ingestion Budget dashboard's own panel, filtered to this one tenant. Queried via the Mimir-anonymous datasource, not Mimir-1229-${env} - see README.md's Multi-Tenancy section for why (self-monitoring metrics land under the anonymous tenant).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-anonymous",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 17,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 120,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 80
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "expr": "100 * demo_ingestion_since_midnight{tenant=~\"1229-${env}\"} / on(tenant, signal) demo_ingestion_daily_budget{tenant=~\"1229-${env}\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{signal}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "title": "Windows Hosts",
      "description": "No target_info for this tenant (unlike Linux Basis), so this is derived from Processor_Processor_Time_ratio's per-core instance labels instead - one row per host, count = logical CPU cores. See the OS Release pie charts below for release/version.",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 10,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {
              "host_name": "Host",
              "Value": "CPU Cores"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count by (host_name) (Processor_Processor_Time_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"})",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "title": "CPU Utilization by Host",
      "description": "Averaged across logical cores per host.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 10,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "avg by (host_name) (Processor_Processor_Time_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "title": "Available Memory by Host",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 17,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "decmbytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "Memory_Available_MBytes_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "title": "OS Release by Major Version",
      "description": "Lifecycle overview: how many hosts are on which Windows Server release. os_name is already the major-level grouping (e.g. \"Windows Server 2022\") - Windows doesn't have a Linux-style major.minor split, so no regex extraction is needed here unlike linux-host's equivalent panel.",
      "type": "piechart",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": [
            "value",
            "percent"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "count by (os_name) (Processor_Processor_Time_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\", instance=\"0\", os_name!=\"\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{os_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "title": "OS Release by Version",
      "description": "One level below major version: exact build (e.g. \"Windows Server 2022 Build 20348\") - the closest Windows equivalent of Linux's exact-version pie chart.",
      "type": "piechart",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": [
            "value",
            "percent"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "count by (os_release) (label_join(Processor_Processor_Time_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\", instance=\"0\", os_name!=\"\"}, \"os_release\", \" Build \", \"os_name\", \"os_version\"))",
          "legendFormat": "{{os_release}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "title": "Disk Free Space by Host/Drive",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "LogicalDisk_Free_Space_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}} {{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "title": "Disk I/O by Host/Drive",
      "description": "Already a per-second rate from the Windows perf counter itself, not a raw counter - no PromQL rate() needed.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "LogicalDisk_Disk_Reads_sec_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}} {{instance}} reads"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "LogicalDisk_Disk_Writes_sec_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}} {{instance}} writes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "title": "Network Throughput by Host/Interface",
      "description": "Already a per-second rate from the Windows perf counter itself - no PromQL rate() needed.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "Network_Interface_Bytes_Total_sec_ratio{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}} {{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "title": "Windows Event Log: Error",
      "description": "Count of Error-level Windows Event Log entries (System/Application channel) over time. This is the signal UC2's own alert (1229 Print Spooler service crashed) watches - see alerting/platforms/1229-windows-basis/alert-rules.yaml, which links back to this exact panel via __panelId__.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Loki-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\".+\"} | detected_level=\"ERROR\" [$__interval])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Error"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "title": "Windows Event Log: Information",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Loki-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 39,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\".+\"} | detected_level=\"INFO\" [$__interval])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "Information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Recent Logs",
      "description": "Queries by service_name, not k8s_namespace_name - this is a VM, not a Kubernetes pod, so it has no k8s_* labels at all.",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": "Loki-1229-${env}",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{service_name=~\".+\"}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
